Z||000000||doughboySE||08-07-2000||01:24 AM||||ok here is my problem. i have my fan hooked into my driving lights. because of this i can run the fan whenever i wish. the problem im having right now is that i am still over heating or very close to it while driving in the city, with the fan on. i dont understand this sometimes i can let the car idle with the fan on for 30 min,then as soon as i move with the fan on the temp rises? what could this be? i have to drive 3 hours sat to newmarket and back and dont want to over heat.<BR>PLEASE HELP<BR>doughboy<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-07-2000||02:27 AM||||Phew, man it could be anything....may need to be refilled w/ coolant,water....may need a new stat, water pump may be sh*tting itself, radiator may be clogged, or, temp. sensors may be bad...if anyone of these things are bad, then a fan isnt going to help too much.....||||reg||1
Z||000002||Archie||08-07-2000||07:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by doughboySE:<BR><B>ok here is my problem. i have my fan hooked into my driving lights. <BR>PLEASE HELP<BR>doughboy</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Did this problem start when you hooked the fan up to the driving lights?<P>Sounds like to run the radiator fan you flip on the driving lights, right?<P>Did you ever consider that the driving lights are pulling power from the fan motor and that the fan is not running as fast as it would without the driving lights on the same circuit?<P>Just a thought.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||08-07-2000||02:48 PM||||You rang, Doughboy?  I was about to start mocking you and say something totally sarcastic, but then I realized that it's counter-productive and just downright mean.  Soooo.... I'll be helpful and recommend that you check your coolant level!  Make sure the system is full and maybe try a 180 degree stat.  While it idles, make sure there are NO leaks under the car.  BTW--- you missed some periods in your origional post.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
