Z||000007||doughboySE||08-07-2000||09:35 PM||||ok here is what i tried tonight.<BR>i took out the stat and put it in a boiling pot of water. the stat did not do anything . does this mean that the stat is shot?<BR>i also checked the fan and its blowing into the rad i can feel it blowing through from the other side of the rad.<BR>one other thing i tried tonight was to drive without the fan running at all times( this is what i do on a reg basis that way i thought i didnt have to worry about overheating). but it looks to me that the fan only works right if its running and the car is ideling ie.in my driveway as i run into the house for a bit, if i do this the fan keeps the car under half way on the temp gage. but what i found out tonight is that if i drive and dont run the fan while i drive, the car dosnt even reach half way on the gage <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> i would imagine thats why the fan dosnt run as the car is in motion am i right?<BR>please correct me if im wrong im running short on time||||reg||1
Z||000008||hugh||08-07-2000||09:54 PM||||It sure sounds as if your fan is running backwards.Your thermostat should open all the way when in boiling water.If it did nothing your car should overheat no matter what conditions you are running the engine under.It may be partially open.Take a piece of toilet tissue or a light piece of paper and hold it in front of the fan while it is running,it should blow away from the fan.If it is drawn into the fan,It's running backwards.To reverse the direction you need to reverse the two wires supplying the fan.Hope this helps. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||doughboySE||08-07-2000||10:46 PM||||HUGH you are right man i did that before i did that post and it sucked the paper toward the fan so will this make a really big difference? as far as running hot? would this blow codes? does it make the car run shitty? thanx hugh im on the right track now||||reg||1
