Z||000012||daved||08-08-2000||11:14 PM||||Hey Doughboy,<BR>I had overheating problems and it turned out to be a leak in the rad cap.  Cheapest fix I ever did! No pressure means it boils at 212 deg F, or 100 deg C.  15 psi of pressure and she wont boil till say 240 deg. F. (depends on the mix of water/glycol)<BR>BTW, water is a better conductor of heat, but tends to get solid in our winters!<BR>Also when I got my car, the previous owner had somehow gotten the thermostat in sideways (very difficult to do), which gave me the opposite problem...she never warmed up on cold days.<BR>It does sound like your thermostat is Kaput.  Also a cheap repair. <BR>And how did the fan rotation get reversed?<BR>Hope you fix it in time for your road trip...and it's going to be very hot for the next few days,  Good luck, Dave||||reg||1
Z||000013||daved||08-08-2000||11:19 PM||||Hey Doughboy,<BR>I had overheating problems and it turned out to be a leak in the rad cap.  Cheapest fix I ever did! No pressure means it boils at 212 deg F, or 100 deg C.  15 psi of pressure and she wont boil till say 240 deg. F. (depends on the mix of water/glycol)<BR>BTW, water is a better conductor of heat, but tends to get solid in our winters!<BR>Also when I got my car, the previous owner had somehow gotten the thermostat in sideways (very difficult to do), which gave me the opposite problem...she never warmed up on cold days.<BR>It does sound like your thermostat is Kaput.  Also a cheap repair. <BR>And how did the fan rotation get reversed?<BR>Hope you fix it in time for your road trip...and it's going to be very hot for the next few days,  Good luck, Dave||||reg||1
